🧠 Data Science Real-World Projects in Python

This repository contains four real-world Data Science mini projects implemented in Python, each focused on different domains — Machine Learning, NLP, AI, and Time Series Forecasting.  
Each project is organized into its own branch.


📂 Projects Overview:

🚀 Airline Tickets Prediction (https://github.com/kledihaxhimali/Data-Science-Projects/tree/Airline-Tickets-Prediction)
Domain: Regression / Machine Learning  
Goal: Predict airline ticket prices based on various flight-related features.  
Workflow:
- Data collection and cleaning  
- Feature engineering and preprocessing  
- Model training and evaluation  
- Visualization and insights  


🎬 Movie Recommendation System (https://github.com/kledihaxhimali/Data-Science-Projects/tree/Movie-Recommendation)
Domain: NLP / Recommendation Systems  
Goal: Recommend similar movies based on content similarity.  
Workflow:
- Data loading and text processing  
- Feature extraction using vectorization  
- Similarity computation and ranking  
- Generating recommendations  


🔐 Password Strength Prediction (https://github.com/kledihaxhimali/Data-Science-Projects/tree/Password-Prediction)
Domain: Classification / NLP  
Goal: Predict the strength level of passwords (weak, medium, or strong).  
Workflow:
- Data preparation and feature extraction  
- Model selection and training  
- Performance evaluation using metrics  
- Visualization and reporting  


💹 Stock Prices Forecasting (https://github.com/kledihaxhimali/Data-Science-Projects/tree/Stock-Prices)
Domain: Time Series Forecasting  
Goal: Forecast stock price movements using statistical and deep learning models.  
Workflow:
- Data collection and preprocessing  
- Exploratory time series analysis  
- Model building (ARIMA, LSTM, Prophet)  
- Forecast visualization and performance comparison  

🧰 Tools & Technologies

A range of tools and technologies were applied across the projects, each supporting different stages of the data science workflow.

Programming & Analysis
-Python, Jupyter Notebook

Data Processing
-Pandas, NumPy

Data Visualization
-Matplotlib, Seaborn
-Plotly (interactive dashboards and charts)

Machine Learning
-Scikit-learn (classification, clustering, model evaluation)
